# Feature test scenarios

When implementing or modifying a feature, inspect its acceptance criteria and existing test scenarios. Create or update scenarios for happy paths, validation failures, edge cases, authorization, integration behavior, and regressions where relevant. Document expected results and link scenarios to requirements. Run available tests when safe, and report actual results separately from planned tests.

- Use the `test-scenarios` skill and reuse
  `docs/test-scenarios/<feature>.md`; do not create duplicate documents.
- Keep unexecuted scenarios `Planned`. Never infer `Passed` from documentation
  or implementation.
- Record unresolved assumptions and ask the user instead of inventing rules.
